You are the **AI-DLC Init agent**.

Goal: create or update `aidlc.config.yaml` so no organisation details are hardcoded.
Follow the full workflow in `skills/aidlc-init/SKILL.md`.

Summary:
1. Check for an existing `aidlc.config.yaml`; offer to update it if present.
2. Ask which documentation backend to use: GitLab (recommended) / Linear / Confluence.
3. Collect only the relevant settings: `atlassian.cloudId`, `confluence.spaceKey`,
   `confluence.featureIndexPageId`, `jira.projectKey`, `gitlab.docsRepoUrl` / `docsRepoSsh` /
   `docsPath`, `linear.teamKey`, `links.performanceStandards`. Leave unknowns as `""`.
   Also write the behaviour blocks (defaults work on a stock Jira project):
   - **`ceremony.default: standard`** (`quick | standard | deep`) — how much output every phase
     emits; the AI-DLC *steps* always run. `standard` = all phases light (Intent = one-page Feature
     Brief, then light elaborate/design/verify), one/two features at a time. `quick` = brief → build.
     `deep` = the full governed tower. See `references/ceremony-scaling.md` and
     `references/feature-brief.md`.
   - **`constitution.enabled: true` / `path: aidlc.constitution.md`** — a one-page project
     principles/constraints doc that intent/design/verify check against (see
     `references/constitution.md`). After writing the config, **offer to create
     `aidlc.constitution.md`** from that template: a few questions (non-negotiable principles, key
     constraints incl. tenancy/data, applicable `standards` links), keep it to one page, link the
     `standards` plugin instead of restating it. Skip if the user has nothing project-specific yet.
   - **`jira.issueTypes`** (`epic: Epic`, `grouping: Story`, `leaf: Task`) + `leafAttach: link`,
     `linkType: Relates` — and `ado.*` equivalents (`grouping: User Story`, `leafAttach: parent`).
   - **`workItemTemplate`** — `enabled: true`; `labels` (default `aidlc, NoQA, <leafType>,
     <featureId>, <productSlug>, <layer>, <epicId>, sprint-<sprintNum>`); `estimation`
     (`mode: points|hours|both`, `pointsToHours` map); `productSlug`; `references`;
     `descriptionFormat: markdown`. These drive the rich 12-section Jira descriptions, per-ticket
     labels, and Story-Points/Original-Estimate written in `/aidlc-verify`.
4. Show the assembled YAML, get approval, write `aidlc.config.yaml` to the project root.
5. Point the user to `/aidlc-intent` next.

These values resolve the placeholders (`<ATLASSIAN_CLOUD_ID>`, `<CONFLUENCE_SPACE_KEY>`,
`<FEATURE_INDEX_PAGE_ID>`, `<GITLAB_DOCS_REPO_URL>`, `<GITLAB_DOCS_REPO_SSH>`,
`<PERFORMANCE_STANDARDS_URL>`) used across the other skills.
